  "title": "Remove Element",
  "summary": "Given an integer array nums and an integer val, remove all occurrences of val from nums in-place.",
  "statement": "Given an integer array nums and an integer val, remove all occurrences of val from nums in-place. The order of the elements in the modified array does not need to be preserved. Return the count of elements in nums that are not equal to val. Ensure that the first k elements of nums contain the elements not equal to val, and the remaining elements can be anything. Return k.",
  "constraints": [
    "0–100 entries with values 0–50; val is between 0 and 100.",
    "Modify nums so its first k entries contain every original value unequal to val, and return k. Prefix order is unrestricted; multiplicity must be preserved.",
    "The judge shows {return, prefix}. It ignores the list tail and permits resizing, but returning another list without updating nums does not satisfy the contract."
  ],
