  "hints": [
    "Every original occurrence unequal to val must survive, including duplicates.",
    "Compact survivors toward the front with a write index.",
    "For each value different from val, assign nums[write]=value and increment write; return write.",
    "Do not remove from the list while blindly advancing a read index, which can skip shifted values."
  ],
  "editorial": "Copy each surviving value to the next write position. Since writes never move ahead of the current read position, unread values are preserved. This stable reference also satisfies the more permissive any-order contract. The oracle filters a separate list, while the judge compares the returned count and the modified prefix as a multiset, retaining duplicate counts.",
